# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Secrets — these must NEVER reach a public repository.
#  Git history is permanent. A key committed once is a key that is burned,
#  even if the next commit deletes it. Bots scrape public repos within minutes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
key.properties
keystore.properties
.env
.env.*
secrets.dart
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Machine-specific paths. These point at where the SDK lives on THIS laptop,
#  which is meaningless — and mildly revealing — on anyone else's.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app/android/local.properties
app/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
app/ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Build output. Regenerated by `flutter build`, so committing it would just
#  add hundreds of megabytes of noise that goes stale immediately.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/app/debug/
app/android/app/profile/
app/android/app/release/
app/ios/Pods/
app/ios/.symlinks/
app/ios/Runner.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.iml
*.ipa
*.apk
*.aab

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Editor and operating-system clutter.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Test and scratch output. A vault written by a test contains no real notes,
#  but there is no reason for one to travel, and a stray *.vault in the repo
#  would be confusing to anyone reading it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
*.vault
scratch/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SCREENSHOT_HOLE — screenshots pulled off the phone by tool/shot.ps1.
#  These are pictures of the app with real notes on the screen. They are the
#  one kind of plaintext this repo could plausibly leak, so they never get
#  committed, even after the hole itself is closed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
shots/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Microsoft Office lock files.
#
#  Word writes `~$Name.docx` and a `~WRLnnnn.tmp` beside any document that is
#  open, and deletes them when it closes — usually. Two of them were sitting in
#  `Thought Process/` on 22 August because the issues document had been open
#  while the repo was committed. They are not content and they confuse anyone
#  who lists that directory looking for the real files.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
~$*
~WRL*.tmp
*.tmp

# A scratch TEMP directory on the same drive as the repo.
#
# flutter test on this machine cannot load libsodium's DLL when TEMP is on a
# different drive from the worktree, so runs set TMP/TEMP to a folder here.
# It is machine-local working space and has no business in the history.
.tmpclaude/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  `Thought Process/` USED TO BE IGNORED HERE. It is tracked on purpose now,
#  decided by Piyush on 28 August 2026, and this note is what it was replaced
#  with so nobody re-adds the rule believing it was an oversight.
#
#  The argument for ignoring it was that `PLAN.md` §12 and
#  `05-shipping/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md` both plan for the source to go public,
#  git history is permanent, and photographs of somebody's own journal — with
#  their own writing on the screen — are not part of the source of an app.
#  That argument was sound and it is still sound *for a public repository*.
#
#  His answer, verbatim: *"my github is private only and will stay private the
#  whole life."* Given that, the balance goes the other way, and it is not a
#  close call: those 82 files are 84 MB of his own handwritten feedback and
#  they existed in exactly one place on earth — this laptop. A private
#  repository is a real backup for them, and the laptop is not.
#
#  **What this does NOT license.** If the repository is ever made public, this
#  directory has to come out of the history first — which means rewriting it,
#  not deleting the files in a new commit. `05-shipping/GOING-PUBLIC.md` carries
#  that as a blocker. And it changes nothing about rule 9: keystores and
#  `key.properties` stay out of a private repository too, because a signing key
#  that leaks lets somebody else ship an update over the top of this app.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#  `kofi_brandasset/` is gone from disk entirely — the Ko-fi mark was deleted
#  in round eight's ISSUE 9, because an unused trademark in the APK is a claim
#  the app is not making. Nothing to ignore and nothing to track.

# Store assets, generated by app/tool/generate_store_assets_test.dart. Build
# products with a one-line recipe; a repository is not an asset library.
app/store/
